2026-06-05 07:22:06,477 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] Findings span only **2 kill chain phases**: Initial Access (T1133) and Credential Access (T1110.001). No progression to Execution, Persistence, Privilege Escalation, Defense Evasion, Lateral Movement, Collection, Exfiltration, or C2. This is fully consistent with an **unsuccessful brute-force attack**.
2026-06-05 07:22:06,479 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Counter-Evidence Findings
2026-06-05 07:22:06,480 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q1 — Active Account Last Login (STRENGTHENS conclusion):** SAM data definitively shows srl-h last logged in on 2020-11-10 and fredr on 2020-11-14 — both BEFORE the 11/16 attack. If an attacker had guessed either password, the Last Login timestamp would have updated. This is the single strongest piece of evidence confirming no compromise. Updated findings f_ef85e9ae and f_07feac45.
2026-06-05 07:22:06,482 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q2 — Security.evtx gap:** Confirmed as an evidentiary gap, not evidence of tampering. The active log was not found in the extraction. The gap is now fully mitigated by the SAM Last Login evidence.
2026-06-05 07:22:06,483 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q3 — CobaltStrike_MZ_Launcher YARA:** Byte pattern `4D 5A 41 52 55 48 89 E5 48 81 EC 20 00 00 00 48 8D 1D` is a standard MZ PE header + x86-64 function prologue. Confirmed false positive — ubiquitous in legitimate Windows memory.
2026-06-05 07:22:06,485 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q4 — Hayabusa claim (CORRECTED):** Hayabusa was never run. Finding f_07feac45 incorrectly stated "No Hayabusa alerts." Corrected to note the tool wasn't run, and the archived EVTXs predate the attack anyway.
